        "faqs": [
          {
            "question": "What Is the Proper Mounting Type Needed for Circuit Board Implementation?",
            "answer": "This connector utilizes a right-angle, surface-mount (SMD) design. During implementation, it should be placed on the edge of the PCB to allow proper external cable insertion, and standard SMT reflow soldering processes should be followed."
          },
          {
            "question": "What Are the Key Technical Specifications Regarding Power and Temperature Limits?",
            "answer": "This right-angle female Type-C connector features a voltage rating of 20V and a current rating of 5A. It is designed to operate reliably within a temperature range of -30°C to +80°C."
          },
          {
            "question": "What Are the Primary Application Scenarios for This Particular Connector?",
            "answer": "Thanks to its compact surface-mount design and robust 5A current rating, this connector is ideal for modern electronic devices requiring power delivery and standard data transfer, such as smartphones, IoT modules, power banks, and portable consumer electronics."
          },
          {
            "question": "How Can I Find Alternative or Replacement Connectors With Similar Specifications on LCSC?",
            "answer": "You can easily find suitable replacements by clicking the \"Show similar products\" link on the product page. This allows you to filter through over 7,000 alternative USB Type-C connector assemblies based on your specific mounting or packaging requirements."
          },
          {
            "question": "Is This USB Type-C Receptacle Fully Compatible With Standard 24-Pin USB-C Cables?",
            "answer": "Yes, it is fully compatible. While this connector has a 16-pin layout physically soldered to the board (optimizing space and cost for power and USB 2.0 data applications), it interfaces seamlessly with standard 24-pin USB Type-C cables."
          }
